`catch (e: CancellationException) { throw e }` is exactly what the repo's exception-discipline rule asks for, and it is right almost everywhere. It is wrong **directly around a `withTimeout`**, because there the cancellation is *the callee's own signal*, not the caller's — the same distinction #2285 just promoted to the top of the rule in `CLAUDE.md` (*whose cancellation is this?*). `currentCorout

